sequenceDiagram
%% Maps to EA diagram: UML Sequence (conceptual overview)
%% Simplified: ERSys collapsed to single ERS lifeline

participant Originator as "Originator"
participant ERS as "Entity Resolution Service (ERS)"
participant MessagingMiddleware as "Messaging Middleware"
participant ERE as "Entity Resolution Engine (ERE)"

%% Phase 1 — Bounded intake (synchronous)
Originator ->> ERS: Resolve Entity Mention<br/>(request identifiers + EntityMention)
ERS ->> ERS: Validate and register request (idempotent)
ERS ->> ERS: Derive deterministic canonical identifier<br/>and ensure Resolution Decision exists
ERS -->> Originator: Draft canonical identifier <br/>+ status (bounded)

%% Phase 2 — Automated assessment (asynchronous)
ERS ->> MessagingMiddleware: Publish resolution request<br/>(request identifiers + EntityMention)
MessagingMiddleware ->> ERE: Deliver request (async)
ERE ->> MessagingMiddleware: Publish resolution response <br/>(candidates + confidence scores)
MessagingMiddleware ->> ERS: Deliver results (async)
ERS ->> ERS: Integrate candidates <br> under decision-centric governance

%% Phase 3 — Convergence (read-only observation)
Originator ->> ERS: Lookup canonical assignment<br/>(sourceId, requestId, entityType)
ERS -->> Originator: Current canonical identifier + status
